       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A dose of 6,000 mg/day is about 50% above the 4,000 mg/day maximum. It could cause acute liver injury even in a patient with normal liver function, and I don't know of any clinical scenario that calls for it. You also haven't given a rationale. Entering it as written would put the patient at real risk of harm.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Order a safe dose now.** I can enter 1000 mg by mouth three times daily (3,000 mg/day) or four times daily (4,000 mg/day) right away.\n- **Check with pharmacy.** If you think this dose is intended, for example as part of a protocol I'm not aware of, a pharmacist can review it. The order may also need to go through your institution's override process.\n- **Check for a typo.** The intended dose may have been 1000 mg or 650 mg.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
